# Regression fixture (docs/projects/ai_tooling_next_steps.md): a factored
# nullable, non-empty suffix (WS?) that is NOT trailing-fallback-
# equivalent. The unit after it is a live guarded suffix (NUMBER), not a
# dead strict epsilon, so pg_choice_unit_is_nullable_fallback does not
# exempt it: the WS? unit has no committed dispatch (it matches on every
# token while NUMBER still expects a turn), and emitting it anyway is the
# shape that once segfaulted the streaming emitter on a missing guard
# set. pg_report_choice must reject it at generation time; the build step
# asserts both diagnostics (the no-committed-dispatch line and the
# first-set overlap pair). The trailing-fallback-equivalent twin of this
# grammar -- dead epsilon instead of the NUMBER suffix -- is accepted and
# pinned by streaming_fallback_sample.pg.
parser edge_probe
mode streaming
token IDENT letters
token NUMBER digits
token WS = [ \t]+
start value
rule value = IDENT WS? | IDENT NUMBER
